Wave 1 complete no leaks, gold 342 (260 + kills 40 + bonus 42 = 342). Good. 45s may include waiting at end but fine.

Now balance simulation with policy. Need play all 20 waves automatically, upgrade/swap. We can implement in eval; game.advance runs update. Need note UI events not rendered but sync. We can script:
```
n.start();
for(wave=1..20){
  // strategy before wave
  ...
  n.startWave();
  let guard=0;
  while(ui.mode==='wave' && guard<120){ n.advance(1); guard++; spend(); }
}
```
But each advance(1) returns after 1s. Spending needs current gold. Strategy:
- Upgrade when affordable, keep certain reserve for swap.
- Swap to specific forms at waves: e.g. pulse wave1-2, mortar 3-5, blaze 6-8, tesla 9-12, rail 13-20? But all forms same level and costs. Strategy could upgrade mostly.
- Auto choose form by wave with some heuristic: <4 pulse, <7 mortar, <10 cryo? Hmm need test each.
Let's first just simulate with upgrade only pulse to see if winnable and where fails. This tests baseline.

Script:
```
n.start();
const log=[];
for(let w=1; w<=20; w++){
  let guard=0;
  while(n.getUI().mode==='prep' && guard<20){
     const u=n.getUI();
     if(u.upgradeCost!==null && u.gold>=u.upgradeCost) n.upgrade(); else break;
     guard++;
  }
  if(!n.startWave()) break;
  let t=0;
  while(n.getUI().mode==='wave' && t<90){ n.advance(1); t++; 
     // upgrade during wave if affordable
     const u=n.getUI();
     if(u.upgradeCost!==null && u.gold>=u.upgradeCost) n.upgrade();
  }
  const u=n.getUI();
  log.push({w:u.wave, mode:u.mode,lives:u.lives,gold:u.gold,level:u.level,form:u.form});
  if(u.mode!=='prep') break;
}
return log;
```
This upgrades immediately whenever affordable, which may leave no gold for swaps but pulse-only. Let's test.

